1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete and coherent: it shows a healthy pre-restart state, accepted restart scheduling, an intervening loss of connectivity, a changed boot identity, a running recovered system, matching persisted data, and restored access controls. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["Collaboration behavior used one simulated member UID with the platform GID rather than two distinct named members editing the same file; directory permissions, setgid inheritance, and the observed group-writable file nevertheless directly support the required shared-workspace behavior.","The restart acknowledgement proves successful scheduling rather than a provider API acknowledgement, although the subsequent disconnect, changed boot ID, and recovered state directly establish that the restart occurred."]}
